WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.560
Right up front, I use the word:

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:09.150
and those are all perfectly good biological words

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:11.280
associated with structures and behaviors

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:14.760
that fulfill an absolutely critical biological role.

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:17.200
Certainly there are people who might be

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:19.920
taken aback a little bit, surprised.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.980
But I tell you, once i actually tell people that

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:25.740
I study genitalia and that I look at penises and vaginas,

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:28.460
I have never had anybody say:

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:31.400
"Oh my gosh, that sounds terrible."

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:34.080
Or be bored for any amount of time.

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:36.059
I mean they  all just want to sit there and hear these

00:00:36.059 --> 00:00:38.129
incredible stories about how animals

00:00:38.129 --> 00:00:41.100
actually go about the business of having sex.

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:47.649
My name is Patty Brennan

00:00:47.649 --> 00:00:49.680
and  I'm an  evolutionary biologist.

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:51.430
I work at Mount Holyoke College

00:00:51.430 --> 00:00:53.130
in the Department of Biological Sciences.

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:57.081
I'm interested in a wide group of vertebrates.

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:59.489
So we have been collecting many animals.

00:00:59.489 --> 00:01:02.080
The work I do is essentially evolutionary morphology

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:03.840
So, I need to be able to describe

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:05.420
what the genitalia looks like.

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:08.520
So, dissections of animals and structures.

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:09.860
We can actually make molds.

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:12.780
Then look at the histology:

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:14.790
just the basic architecture of the tissue.

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:17.130
And then I need to know how they work, so I've been

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:19.820
testing the material properties of vaginas.

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:22.420
But because they don't function independently

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:25.350
then i also need to know how the genitals function

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:26.650
with each other.

00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:27.920
That means 3D models and

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:29.540
essentially use that to predict then

00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:33.500
what are the structures that are under selection

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:34.979
for evolution to actually take place

00:01:34.979 --> 00:01:37.319
and end up with this:

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:44.280
So these are the mako shark.

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:46.860
And so the males have these genitals attached to

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:49.619
their pelvic fins and when the males are

00:01:49.619 --> 00:01:52.499
going to copulate they typical use only one of these.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:53.760
So they'll use one clasper.

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:56.480
So the clasper will go in the female.

00:01:56.490 --> 00:01:59.210
And then, once the male is inside of the female

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:01.400
He will actually pull down on a muscle

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:04.760
and essentially open up the tip of the clasper.

00:02:05.909 --> 00:02:07.920
The tip of that is called a spur.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:09.580
You'll actually feels it's really sharp.

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:11.500
And what that's going to allow him to do

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:14.420
is stay attached until he's able to deliver the sperm.

00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:16.069
Isn't it the most beautiful thing?

00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:18.329
I think this is just really incredibly cool.

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:22.100
Diagrams that I find— there will be like this description

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:25.760
of the claspers but there's nothing at all on the vagina.

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:28.040
Essentially there's very little consideration given to:

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:30.109
" Well where's this clasper actually going

00:02:30.109 --> 00:02:31.939
and what is it doing?"

00:02:31.939 --> 00:02:34.459
And so that surprised me, again in a good way

00:02:34.459 --> 00:02:36.199
because it means that I have

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:37.300
an interesting question to go look at.

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:40.340
So when we have the females we can actually make

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:42.799
molds of the vagina.

00:02:42.799 --> 00:02:45.769
Essentially I use silicone and then I inject the silicone

00:02:45.769 --> 00:02:47.889
so it flows into all the crevices

00:02:47.889 --> 00:02:49.469
and all the spaces of the female.

00:02:50.209 --> 00:02:52.639
We let it cure and then we pull it out and then

00:02:52.639 --> 00:02:55.370
that gives us a 3D image of the

00:02:55.370 --> 00:02:57.500
negative space inside of the vagina.

00:02:57.500 --> 00:03:01.310
Here we have the mako female

00:03:01.310 --> 00:03:03.349
and she was a very large female.

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:04.909
And this is the intestine so from here,

00:03:04.909 --> 00:03:06.780
the intestine would go up that way.

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:09.950
So that clasper most likely is coming in

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:12.180
from the entrance here of the cloaca

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:14.180
and it's probably going right

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:16.340
through this little notch right here.

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:18.500
And then once it gets past that point then

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:21.379
the male pulls out on that clasper muscle

00:03:21.379 --> 00:03:24.260
to open it up and then dig right in there

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:26.209
and just hook itself to the female

00:03:26.209 --> 00:03:28.310
so  that then he can ejaculate and all his sperm

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:30.490
will go up inside of the female tract.

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:34.120
The sharks have these long spines, spurs

00:03:34.129 --> 00:03:36.739
in their claspers but other animals like

00:03:36.739 --> 00:03:39.859
snakes for example they also have spines.

00:03:39.859 --> 00:03:42.169
These are timber rattlesnakes.

00:03:42.169 --> 00:03:45.929
They were run over by cars and so I got these locally.

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:47.599
The three-dimensional shape of the structure

00:03:47.599 --> 00:03:50.739
for the males hasn't been described, so we'll do that.

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:54.360
We're about to inflate the male hemipene so that they

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:57.480
get as close as they can to their functional shape.

00:03:57.480 --> 00:03:59.960
And I'm saying hemipene because like sharks

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:02.140
the snakes have two penises instead of one.

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:05.480
And they'll use one or the other when they're copulating.

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:10.180
Perfect.

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:13.660
This is the mold that we just pulled out of the female.

00:04:15.129 --> 00:04:16.569
We can describe how it's variable,

00:04:16.569 --> 00:04:19.359
we can look at the differences in the shapes.

00:04:19.359 --> 00:04:21.299
So these are all different species of snakes.

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:24.020
We have a rattlesnake, that's the big one we just did.

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:27.360
Then we have a plains garter snake.

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:29.900
And then a python and then a yellow rat snake.

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:33.580
We know that the vaginas need to be elastic

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:36.500
because they're used also for the babies to be born

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:38.020
or the eggs to be laid right?

00:04:38.020 --> 00:04:39.759
But is there anything above and beyond that

00:04:39.759 --> 00:04:43.000
that is the result of actual copulation

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:45.520
and interacting with those spines?

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:47.199
We don't know whether that's the case or not

00:04:47.199 --> 00:04:50.159
in snakes because it hasn't been looked at.

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:52.240
And so one of the things we want to do is

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:54.020
then look at the histology:

00:04:54.580 --> 00:04:56.199
What those tissues are in the females

00:04:56.199 --> 00:04:58.060
but also the thickness and the relative

00:04:58.060 --> 00:05:00.430
proportion of these tissues

00:05:00.430 --> 00:05:01.539
in all these different species.

00:05:01.539 --> 00:05:04.339
This is beautiful, look at that one.

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:07.760
Oh, wow.

00:05:08.180 --> 00:05:11.000
What we can see here is lots of smooth muscle

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:13.800
in the red  and then over here in the blue is

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:15.140
lot's of connective tissue.

00:05:15.140 --> 00:05:18.400
Then we can inflate the male's inside of the female

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:20.260
And we'll put them in a micro CT scanner

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:23.180
And we can get images of

00:05:23.180 --> 00:05:25.720
where the male features end up inside of the female.

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:28.600
And it's obviously not exactly what happens

00:05:28.600 --> 00:05:31.080
during copulation but it's the closest we're going to get

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:33.140
when we look at these large vertebrates.

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:36.720
There's a lot more to discover

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:37.780
in the female side of things

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:39.920
that's going to really help us

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:41.780
understand then the male part of things.

00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:44.380
I mean these have not evolved in a vacuum.

00:05:44.380 --> 00:05:47.780
They have co-evolved so closely—more closely

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:50.820
than any other structure that we can think about.

00:05:51.260 --> 00:05:53.800
For me, I'm really excited about the process

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:56.000
of discovering and so I do actually tend to

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:58.910
seek out areas where there is something

00:05:58.910 --> 00:06:00.890
that is not well understood

00:06:00.890 --> 00:06:03.300
or that we don't have all the details.

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:05.020
That's what happens sometimes in science,

00:06:05.020 --> 00:06:06.500
you just gotta follow the questions

00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:11.780
wherever they take you, and so here I am.

